msgid "Dynamically adjust layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1092
msgid ""
"Balance pass heights on a 0.01 mm grid while preserving the exact local layer height. One pass "
"may carry a 0.001 mm correction. When disabled, only equal 0.01 mm pass heights are used and the "
"pass count is reduced if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1098
msgid "External perimeter pass flow"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1100
msgid ""
"Divide total flow preserves the external perimeter's original total extrusion by distributing it "
"in proportion to pass height. Recompute each pass calculates a new rounded-rectangle cross-"
"section from the original line width and each pass height; total extrusion may increase or "
"decrease, and bridge or overhang segments may differ from their original calibration."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1102
msgid "Divide total flow"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1103
msgid "Recompute each pass"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1110
msgid "Enable Z-curve smoothing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1112
msgid ""
"Move each fine external-perimeter pass to the real mesh contour at the middle of that pass. Inner "
"perimeters and nearby model fill follow the selected reference so the fine surface is not crushed "
"or disconnected. The feature is not used on an object's first model layer, rafts, brim, support, "
"or areas where fine external perimeters fall back to normal printing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1119
msgid "Extend Z-curve ends"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1121
msgid ""
"Continue an ending outer contour into the remaining fine passes when no matching mesh contour "
"exists. The artificial continuation keeps all planned Z heights and is limited to one external-"
"perimeter extrusion width beyond the last valid contour. It may change the shape of the upper "
"surface. Requires Z-curve smoothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1129
msgid "Inner perimeter smoothing reference"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1131
msgid ""
"Selects which fine-pass contour controls inner perimeters and nearby fill. Innermost uses the "
"contour reaching furthest into the material and provides the most conservative collision "
"clearance. Outermost uses the contour furthest away from the material. Average uses a pass-height-"
"weighted mean. Direction extreme evaluates the local contour trend from bottom to top: narrowing "
"areas use Innermost, widening areas use Outermost, and ambiguous or non-monotonic areas blend "
"toward Average."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1134
msgid "Innermost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1135
msgid "Outermost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1136
msgid "Average"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1137
msgid "Direction extreme"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1144
msgid "Inner perimeter smoothing shift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1146
msgid ""
"Scales the displacement of inner perimeters and nearby model fill. 0% leaves them unchanged, 100% "
"follows the selected fine-pass reference, and values above 100% move them further in the same "
"direction. Large extrapolations may create an intentional gap and are limited locally if the "
"resulting geometry would become invalid."
msgstr ""

