#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4478
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for external perimeters. Set zero to use the value "
"for perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4485
msgid "Perimeter extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4487
msgid "The tool to use when printing perimeters and brim. T0 is the first extruder."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4496
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. You may want to use "
"thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If left zero, default extrusion width will be "
"used if set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 200%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4510
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based perimeter extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4522
msgid "Speed for perimeters (contours, aka vertical shells). Set to zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4532
msgid ""
"This option sets the number of perimeters to generate for each layer. Note that Slic3r may "
"increase this number automatically when it detects sloping surfaces which benefit from a higher "
"number of perimeters if the Extra Perimeters option is enabled."
