#. TRN PrintSettings : "Ooze prevention" > "Temperature variation"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5208
msgid ""
"Temperature difference to be applied when an extruder is not active. The value is not used when "
"'idle_temperature' in material settings is defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5218
msgid "Emit temperature commands automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5219
msgid ""
"When enabled, ApiumSlicer will check whether your custom Start G-Code contains G-codes to set "
"extruder, bed or chamber temperature (M104, M109, M140, M190, M141 and M191). If so, the "
"temperatures will not be emitted automatically so you're free to customize the order of heating "
"commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"ApiumSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want.\n"
"If your custom Start G-Code does NOT contain these G-codes, ApiumSlicer will execute the Start G-"
"Code after heated chamber was set to its temperature, bed reached its target temperature and "
"extruder just started heating.\n"
"\n"
"When disabled, ApiumSlicer will NOT emit commands to heat up extruder, bed or chamber, leaving "
"all to Custom Start G-Code."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5234
msgid "Force temperature integers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5235
msgid ""
"When enabled, supported nozzle, bed and chamber temperature commands in generated and custom G-"
"code are rounded to whole numbers during export. This includes firmware-specific commands and "
"preview slider entries. Klipper always enforces integer temperatures. The original custom G-code "
"and slider entries remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

