msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5914 src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoCut.cpp:240
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoEmboss.cpp:2775
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5916
msgid ""
"Style and shape of the support towers. Projecting the supports into a regular grid will create "
"more stable supports, while snug support towers will save material and reduce object scarring."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5921 src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoFdmSupports.cpp:82
msgid "Snug"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5922 src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoFdmSupports.cpp:84
msgid "Organic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5923
msgid "Framing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5929
msgid "Synchronize with object layers"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings : "Synchronize with object layers"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5932
msgid ""
"Synchronize support layers with the object print layers. This is useful with multi-material "
"printers, where the extruder switch is expensive. This option is only available when top contact "
"Z distance is set to zero."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5939
msgid "Overhang threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5941
msgid ""
"Support material will not be generated for overhangs whose slope angle (90° = vertical) is above "
"the given threshold. In other words, this value represent the most horizontal slope (measured "
"from the horizontal plane) that you can print without support material. Set to zero for automatic "
"detection (recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5953
msgid "With sheath around the support"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5955
msgid ""
"Add a sheath (a single perimeter line) around the base support. This makes the support more "
"reliable, but also more difficult to remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5961
msgid "Maximum Branch Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Maximum Branch Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5964
msgid ""
"The maximum angle of the branches, when the branches have to avoid the model. Use a lower angle "
"to make them more vertical and more stable. Use a higher angle to be able to have more reach."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5973
msgid "Preferred Branch Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Preferred Branch Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5976
msgid ""
"The preferred angle of the branches, when they do not have to avoid the model. Use a lower angle "
"to make them more vertical and more stable. Use a higher angle for branches to merge faster."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5985
msgid "Tip Diameter"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Tip Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5988
msgid "Branch tip diameter for organic supports."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5996
msgid "Branch Diameter"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5999
msgid ""
"The diameter of the thinnest branches of organic support. Thicker branches are more sturdy. "
"Branches towards the base will be thicker than this."
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: #lmFIXME
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6009
msgid "Branch Diameter Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6012
msgid ""
"The angle of the branches' diameter as they gradually become thicker towards the bottom. An angle "
"of 0 will cause the branches to have uniform thickness over their length. A bit of an angle can "
"increase stability of the organic support."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6022
msgid "Branch Diameter with double walls"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6025
msgid ""
"Branches with area larger than the area of a circle of this diameter will be printed with double "
"walls for stability. Set this value to zero for no double walls."
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: #lmFIXME
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6038
msgid "Branch Distance"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Distance"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6041
msgid ""
"How far apart the branches need to be when they touch the model. Making this distance small will "
"cause the tree support to touch the model at more points, causing better overhang but making "
"support harder to remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6048
msgid "Branch Density"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Density"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6051
msgid ""
"Adjusts the density of the support structure used to generate the tips of the branches. A higher "
"value results in better overhangs but the supports are harder to remove, thus it is recommended "
"to enable top support interfaces instead of a high branch density value if dense interfaces are "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6063
msgid ""
"Nozzle temperature for layers after the first one. Set this to zero to disable temperature "
"control commands in the output G-code."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6074
msgid ""
"Enable the per-line-type nozzle temperature target while preserving the stored value when "
"disabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6080
msgid ""
"Nozzle temperature for this extrusion line type. Enter an absolute temperature such as 210, a "
"signed offset such as +10 or -20, or a signed percentage such as +15% or -10%. Relative values "
"use the preceding temperature stage as their base. Values 0, +0, -0, +0% and -0% leave the base "
"unchanged. Percentage offsets are limited to +/-200%, and the result is clamped to the material "
"extrusion temperature limits. Automatic line-type control is disabled when the normal material "
"temperature is 0 or automatic temperature commands are disabled. Frequent changes may be too fast "
"for the printer's thermal response."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6088
msgid ""
"Resolution order: layer base, line type, object, winning modifier geometry, then cumulative "
"slider ticks."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6089
msgid "°C or %"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6096
msgid ""
"Enable the per-line-type part-cooling fan target while preserving the stored value when disabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6102
msgid ""
"Part-cooling fan speed for this extrusion line type. Enter an absolute percentage such as 40, a "
"signed offset such as +10 or -20, or a signed percentage such as +15% or -10%. An absolute 0 "
"turns the fan off, while signed zero leaves the preceding target unchanged. Relative values use "
"the preceding fan stage as their base, percentage offsets are limited to +/-200%, and resolved "
"line-type targets are clamped to 0-100%."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6108
msgid ""
"Resolution order: calculated cooling target, line type, object, winning modifier geometry, then "
"cumulative slider ticks."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6109
msgid "% or +/-"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6115
msgid "Overhang perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6115
msgid "Top solid fill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6116
msgid "Bottom fill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6116
msgid "Solid fill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6117 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:2509
msgid "Support interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6117 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:2452
msgid "Raft"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6117
msgid "Raft interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6127
msgid "Thick bridges"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6129
msgid ""
"If enabled, bridges are more reliable, can bridge longer distances, but may look worse. If "
"disabled, bridges look better but are reliable just for shorter bridged distances."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6135
msgid "Detect thin walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6137
msgid ""
"Detect single-width walls (parts where two extrusions don't fit and we need to collapse them into "
"a single trace)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6144
msgid ""
"This custom code is inserted before every toolchange. Placeholder variables for all ApiumSlicer "
"settings as well as {toolchange_z}, {previous_extruder} and {next_extruder} can be used. When a "
"tool-changing command which changes to the correct extruder is included (such as "
"T{next_extruder}), ApiumSlicer will emit no other such command. It is therefore possible to "
"script custom behaviour both before and after the toolchange."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6157
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for top surfaces. You may "
"want to use thinner extrudates to fill all narrow regions and get a smoother finish. If left "
"zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If "
"expressed as percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6170
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based top solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6182
msgid ""
"Speed for printing top solid layers (it only applies to the uppermost external layers and not to "
"their internal solid layers). You may want to slow down this to get a nicer surface finish. This "
"can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the solid infill speed above. Set to "
"zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#. TRN Print Settings: "Top solid layers"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6195 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6203
msgctxt "Layers"
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6197
msgid "Number of solid layers to generate on top surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6198
msgid "Top solid layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6205
msgid ""
"The number of top solid layers is increased above top_solid_layers if necessary to satisfy "
"minimum thickness of top shell. This is useful to prevent pillowing effect when printing with "
"variable layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6208
msgid "Minimum top shell thickness"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6216
msgid "Speed for travel moves (jumps between distant extrusion points)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6224
msgid "Z travel"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6225
msgid ""
"Speed for movements along the Z axis.\n"
"When set to zero, the value is ignored and regular travel speed is used instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6233
msgid "Use firmware retraction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6234
msgid ""
"This setting uses G10 and G11 commands to have the firmware handle the retraction. Note that this "
"has to be supported by firmware."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6240
msgid "Use relative E distances"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6241
msgid ""
"If your firmware requires relative E values, check this, otherwise leave it unchecked. Most "
"firmwares use absolute values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6247
msgid "Use volumetric E"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6248
msgid ""
"This experimental setting uses outputs the E values in cubic millimeters instead of linear "
"millimeters. If your firmware doesn't already know material diameter(s), you can put commands "
"like 'M200 D[filament_diameter_0] T0' in your start G-code in order to turn volumetric mode on "
"and use the material diameter associated to the material selected in Slic3r. This is only "
"supported in recent Marlin."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6258
msgid "Enable variable layer height feature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6259
msgid ""
"Some printers or printer setups may have difficulties printing with a variable layer height. "
"Enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6265
msgid "Prefer clockwise movements"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6266
msgid "This setting makes the printer print loops clockwise instead of counterclockwise."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6271
msgid "Wipe while retracting"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6272
msgid ""
"This flag will move the nozzle while retracting to minimize the possible blob on leaky extruders."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6279
msgid ""
"Multi material printers may need to prime or purge extruders on tool changes. Extrude the excess "
"material into the wipe tower."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6285
msgid "Purging volumes - matrix"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6286
msgid ""
"This matrix describes volumes (in cubic milimetres) required to purge the new material on the "
"wipe tower for any given pair of tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6305 src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:1260
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoCut.cpp:246
msgid "Width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6306
msgid "Width of a wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6312 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6313
msgid "Wipe tower brim width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6320
msgid "Stabilization cone apex angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6321
msgid ""
"Angle at the apex of the cone that is used to stabilize the wipe tower. Larger angle means wider "
"base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6330
msgid "Wipe tower purge lines spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6331
msgid "Spacing of purge lines on the wipe tower."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6339
msgid "Extra flow for purging"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6340
msgid ""
"Extra flow used for the purging lines on the wipe tower. This makes the purging lines thicker or "
"narrower than they normally would be. The spacing is adjusted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6349 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6357
#: src/slic3r/GUI/GUI_Factories.cpp:111 src/slic3r/GUI/GUI_Factories.cpp:194
msgid "Wipe options"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6350
msgid "Wipe into this object's infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6351
msgid ""
"Purging after toolchange will be done inside this object's infills. This lowers the amount of "
"waste but may result in longer print time  due to additional travel moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6358
msgid "Wipe into this object"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6359
msgid ""
"Object will be used to purge the nozzle after a toolchange to save material that would otherwise "
"end up in the wipe tower and decrease print time. Colours of the objects will be mixed as a "
"result."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6365
msgid "Maximal bridging distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6366
msgid "Maximal distance between supports on sparse infill sections."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6372
msgid "Wipe tower extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6374
msgid ""
"The tool to use when printing perimeter of the wipe tower. Choose 'Current extruder' to use an "
"available tool (non-soluble would be preferred)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6393
msgid "XY Size Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6395
msgid ""
"The object will be grown/shrunk in the XY plane by the configured value (negative = inwards, "
"positive = outwards). This might be useful for fine-tuning hole sizes."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6403
msgid "Z offset"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6404
msgid ""
"This value will be added (or subtracted) from all the Z coordinates in the output G-code. It is "
"used to compensate for bad Z endstop position: for example, if your endstop zero actually leaves "
"the nozzle 0.3mm far from the print bed, set this to -0.3 (or fix your endstop)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6413
msgid "Perimeter generator"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6415
msgid ""
"Classic perimeter generator produces perimeters with constant extrusion width and for very thin "
"areas is used gap-fill. Arachne engine produces perimeters with variable extrusion width. Apium "
"generates interweaving undulating perimeter channels with local robustness fallback. This setting "
"also affects the Concentric infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6421
msgid "Classic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6422
msgid "Arachne"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6423
msgid "Apium"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6429
msgid "Perimeter transition length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6431
msgid ""
"When transitioning between different numbers of perimeters as the part becomes thinner, a certain "
"amount of space is allotted to split or join the perimeter segments. If expressed as a percentage "
"(for example 100%), it will be computed based on the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6440
msgid "Perimeter transitioning filter margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6442
msgid ""
"Prevent transitioning back and forth between one extra perimeter and one less. This margin "
"extends the range of extrusion widths which follow to [Minimum perimeter width - margin, 2 * "
"Minimum perimeter width + margin]. Increasing this margin reduces the number of transitions, "
"which reduces the number of extrusion starts/stops and travel time. However, large extrusion "
"width variation can lead to under- or overextrusion problems. If expressed as a percentage (for "
"example 25%), it will be computed based on the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6455
msgid "Perimeter transitioning threshold angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6457
msgid ""
"When to create transitions between even and odd numbers of perimeters. A wedge shape with an "
"angle greater than this setting will not have transitions and no perimeters will be printed in "
"the center to fill the remaining space. Reducing this setting reduces the number and length of "
"these center perimeters, but may leave gaps or overextrude."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6468
msgid "Perimeter distribution count"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6470
msgid ""
"The number of perimeters, counted from the center, over which the variation needs to be spread. "
"Lower values mean that the outer perimeters don't change in width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6477
msgid "Minimum feature size"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6479
msgid ""
"Minimum thickness of thin features. Model features that are thinner than this value will not be "
"printed, while features thicker than the Minimum feature size will be widened to the Minimum "
"perimeter width. If expressed as a percentage (for example 25%), it will be computed based on the "
"nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6489
msgid "Minimum perimeter width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6491
msgid ""
"Width of the perimeter that will replace thin features (according to the Minimum feature size) of "
"the model. If the Minimum perimeter width is thinner than the thickness of the feature, the "
"perimeter will become as thick as the feature itself. If expressed as a percentage (for example "
"85%), it will be computed based on the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6501
msgid "Wave shape"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6503
msgid ""
"Defines the base curve used for the Apium undulating channel between the anchor shells. "
"Sinusoidal creates smooth transitions with lower dynamic acceleration demand, while Half circle "
"creates steeper local sidewalls and a more pronounced mechanical interlock. This parameter "
"changes the geometric character of contact points and pocket formation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6508
msgid "Sinusoidal"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6509
msgid "Half circle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6515
msgid "Wave steepness"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6517
msgid ""
"Scales how aggressively the Apium wave transitions between crest and valley. Higher values create "
"steeper flanks and stronger geometric locking but increase local acceleration and extrusion "
"stress. Lower values flatten the curve, improving print smoothness and reducing vibration "
"sensitivity."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6526
msgid "Min wave amplitude"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6528
msgid ""
"Lower safety bound for Apium wave amplitude. If local geometry would require a smaller amplitude, "
"the strategy may switch to a local fallback. Keeping this above zero prevents the pattern from "
"degenerating into nearly parallel walls and preserves spring-like stress dissipation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6537
msgid "Max wave amplitude"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6539
msgid ""
"Upper safety bound for Apium wave amplitude. Limits how far the wave bulges toward the shell "
"anchors to avoid self-intersections, excessive path curvature, and unstable extrusion behavior in "
"tight geometry. Increase with caution on rigid mechanics only."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6548
msgid "Min wavelength"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6550
msgid ""
"Minimum allowed wavelength for Apium undulations along a perimeter loop. Shorter wavelengths "
"increase interlock frequency but can amplify jerk, over-segmentation, and flow transients. Use "
"this to enforce a lower bound for dynamic stability."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6559
msgid "Max wavelength"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6561
msgid ""
"Maximum allowed wavelength for Apium undulations. Larger wavelengths smooth the path and reduce "
"directional changes, but if too large they weaken pocket cadence and reduce interlock density. "
"This value caps how stretched the wave may become in thin-wall situations."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6570
msgid "Minimum wave segment length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6572
msgid ""
"Sets the minimum target segment length used by Apium when discretizing wave channels. The value "
"is evaluated as a percentage of the nominal perimeter spacing. Lower values preserve finer "
"curvature detail but generate more G-code segments and can overload motion planners on dense "
"corners. Higher values reduce segment count and improve controller stability at the cost of "
"geometric fidelity."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6583
msgid "Max wave extrusion width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6585
msgid ""
"Hard safety cap for Apium wave extrusion width, expressed as a percentage of nozzle diameter. "
"This limits aggressive width scaling in wide/tight regions and prevents excessive wave line "
"widths that may destabilize pressure control or corner quality."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6595
msgid "Junction detection sensitivity"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6597
msgid ""
"Scales the hybrid Apium junction risk model used to split waves around problematic intersections. "
"Higher values detect and guard more aggressively (including oblique angles), lower values are "
"more conservative and preserve uninterrupted waves in marginal cases."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6607
msgid "Step-over limit"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6609
msgid ""
"Percent threshold controlling when Apium changes internal channel layout for wider walls. The "
"value is evaluated relative to nominal perimeter spacing. Set lower for earlier local fallback on "
"wide geometries, set higher to keep Apium active longer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6618
msgid "Tangential clearance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6620
msgid ""
"Numerical safety clearance used by Apium near wall-contact extrema. The value is evaluated as "
"percent of nozzle diameter. Increase slightly if local clipping becomes unstable; keep low to "
"preserve requested wall overlap geometry."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6629
msgid "Wave wall overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6631
msgid ""
"Controls overlap at wave crest/valley relative to adjacent anchor walls, based on actually "
"extruded strand widths. 0% means strands are side-by-side at the peak (outer sides just touch). "
"100% means full overlap into the wall at the peak. Values above 100% intentionally create outward "
"bulging beyond the anchor wall centerline. The value is evaluated relative to local wall width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6643
msgid "Minimum pocket volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6645
msgid ""
"Minimum target pocket volume for an effective mechanical anchor in adjacent layers. If local "
"pockets collapse below this threshold, Apium may simplify or locally fallback because the rivet "
"effect becomes unreliable. Increase for stronger anchoring criteria, decrease for permissive "
"behavior on fine details."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6654
msgid "Phase mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6656
msgid ""
"Controls vertical phase behavior between adjacent layers. Alternate 180 shifts the pattern by "
"half a period each layer to place crests over valleys for interlock. Fixed uses one static phase "
"offset for all layers and is mainly useful for diagnostics and controlled experiments."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6660
msgid "Alternate 180"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6661
msgid "Fixed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6667
msgid "Fixed phase"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6669
msgid ""
"Phase angle used when phase mode is set to Fixed. Values are interpreted in degrees along the "
"wave period. This is intended for debugging, repeatable A/B testing, and profile characterization."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6672
msgid "deg"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6679
msgid "Enable injection"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6681
msgid ""
"Enables localized flow increase around Apium trigger regions to inject additional material into "
"pockets of the previous layer. This increases vertical mechanical anchoring but may stress hotend "
"pressure dynamics. Disable to evaluate pure geometric interweaving without volumetric purging."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6688
msgid "Injection every N layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6690
msgid ""
"Defines the vertical cadence of Apium injection and phase switching in Alternate 180 mode. Apium "
"keeps the same wave phase for N consecutive layers, then flips phase and injects on the flip "
"layer. This stacks identical wave channels in Z to form deeper pockets before injection, "
"improving mechanical anchoring for high-warping materials. Injected target volume is scaled "
"linearly with N to account for deeper pockets. In Fixed phase mode this setting is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6701
msgid "Injection profile"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6703
msgid ""
"Shape of flow modulation used during Apium injection over the active pocket arc span. Gaussian "
"provides smooth pressure transitions with rounded peak, Trapezoid provides a flatter high-flow "
"plateau with explicit ramp sections."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6707
msgid "Gaussian"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6708
msgid "Trapezoid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6714
msgid "Injection gain"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6716
msgid ""
"Legacy fallback strength for Apium injection when pocket volume multiplier is set to 0%. In "
"normal operation, injected amount should be controlled by the pocket volume multiplier setting. "
"Use this value only for compatibility with older profiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6724
msgid "Injection pocket volume multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6726
msgid ""
"Defines the target injected material volume as a percentage of the estimated lower-layer pocket "
"volume under the current nozzle path. The slicer computes the effective path length above each "
"pocket dynamically and distributes the extra volume along that path using the selected injection "
"profile. 100% targets one estimated pocket volume, values above 100% overfill intentionally, "
"values below 100% inject more conservatively."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6735
msgid "Injection arc coverage"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6737
msgid ""
"Controls how much of the pocket arc width receives injection, centered around each pocket "
"midpoint. For example, 50% means injection is distributed over the middle half of the pocket arc "
"(25% left and 25% right around center). 100% covers the full detected pocket span."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6747
msgid "Flow compensation ratio"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6749
msgid ""
"Scales target injected volume with active wave line width. Use this to keep pocket fill behavior "
"consistent when Apium changes local bead widths due to geometry adaptation. A value of 0 disables "
"width-based compensation, larger values make target volume more width-sensitive."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6757
msgid "Injection sigma"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6759
msgid ""
"Spread parameter of the Gaussian injection profile. Higher sigma broadens and flattens the pulse, "
"lower sigma sharpens it around the trigger center. The value is evaluated per segment relative to "
"the active local half-arc span. Used only when the injection profile is Gaussian."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6769
msgid "Trapezoid ramp"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6771
msgid ""
"Ramp length used for entering and leaving the plateau of a trapezoid injection profile. Longer "
"ramps reduce pressure shocks, shorter ramps produce a more aggressive pulse. The value is "
"evaluated per segment relative to the active local half-arc span. Used only when the injection "
"profile is Trapezoid."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6781
msgid "Max injection multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6783
msgid ""
"Hard upper cap for dynamic flow multiplication during Apium injection. This safety limit prevents "
"excessive volumetric spikes independent of profile shape or gain values. Keep this conservative "
"when material viscosity or hotend throughput is limited."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6791
msgid "Fallback to Arachne"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6793
msgid ""
"Allows local island-level fallback from Apium to Arachne when geometric or robustness constraints "
"cannot be met. This keeps slicing stable and avoids pathological toolpaths in narrow or highly "
"curved regions. Disabling this is recommended only for controlled debugging."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6800
msgid "Disable on small islands"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6802
msgid ""
"Automatically disables Apium on islands with very short perimeter loops where wave construction "
"and injection are less reliable. When enabled, such islands use local fallback behavior to "
"maintain print stability."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6808
msgid "Minimum island perimeter length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6810
msgid ""
"Minimum contour length required for Apium processing when small-island protection is enabled. If "
"an island perimeter is shorter than this value, Apium is skipped locally and fallback rules are "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6818
msgid "W1 contour length factor"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6820
msgid ""
"Robustness factor for odd-slot multiwave layouts that require a W1 channel. The contour must be "
"at least this factor multiplied by nominal spacing, otherwise Apium falls back locally. Higher "
"factors are stricter and favor stability over pattern coverage."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6828
msgid "Debug export SVG"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6830
msgid ""
"Developer diagnostic switch for exporting Apium intermediate geometry data to SVG when available "
"in debug paths. Use this only for algorithm analysis, not for production slicing."
msgstr ""

