#: src/slic3r/GUI/WipeTowerDialog.cpp:66
msgid ""
"Ramming denotes the rapid extrusion just before a tool change in a single-extruder MM printer. "
"Its purpose is to properly shape the end of the unloaded filament so it does not prevent "
"insertion of the new filament and can itself be reinserted later. This phase is important and "
"different materials can require different extrusion speeds to get the good shape. For this "
"reason, the extrusion rates during ramming are adjustable.\n"
"\n"
"This is an expert-level setting, incorrect adjustment will likely lead to jams, extruder wheel "
"grinding into filament etc."
msgstr ""

